# SUMMARY
This document explains how to add a light source to a room, with a switch to control it

# KEY CLASSES
- HighHatLight `GeometryBuilder\Shapes\Appliances\HighHatLight.cs`
	- currently this is the only light source
	- these lights automatically place themselves on the ceiling of their room, at a given X and Z
	- unless told otherwise, place at X=0, Z=0 (default)
- LightSwitch - `GeometryBuilder\Shapes\Appliances\LightSwitch.cs`
	- this is a wall mounted light switch that can control the light
	- I will instruct you on what side of the wall the switch should go on
	- a light switch needs its own StateKey. Every switch should have its own StateKey
	- if you are creating a brand new light, create a new StateKey named after the room it's in
		- be sure to add the new enum value to `LevelControl\GameState.cs`
	- connect a switch to a light using the ControlledObjects collection
	- place the switch by first settings its Position to the Room's position, and then using Place().OnSideInner() to put it on the wall



